With FORCE_COLOR exported (agent harnesses set it), mypy colorizes stdout
even into a pipe. check-mypy-ratchet's trailing-[code] regex then matches
nothing, and the gate reported the 672-error surface as

    whole-tree strict errors = 0 (baseline 672, delta -672)   exit 0

plus "surface shrank — run --update-baseline to lock in the progress".
Taking that advice writes total 0 into the shrink-only baseline and ends
INV-zogud's enforcement with no visible event. A fabricated GROWTH would
merely block; a fabricated SHRINK invites permanently disabling the gate,
which is the most expensive direction a shrink-only instrument can fail.

The failure was environment-dependent: CI runners do not set FORCE_COLOR,
so TestGateFiresForReal (live ratchet must fail an all-zeros baseline)
passed in CI while failing on any harness shell — verified red on
unmodified dev before this fix, exit 0 where the test requires 1. R19's
"smart-test refuses to run pytest over a breach" never fired for the same
reason: the gate saw no breach to refuse over.

Three defences, stacked:

* _run_mypy passes --no-color-output and scrubs FORCE_COLOR /
  MYPY_FORCE_COLOR / CLICOLOR_FORCE from the child env — the live path
  cannot produce colour at all.
* ANSI escapes are stripped before parsing, so a colorized capture fed
  via --input is READ rather than refused.
* Default-deny reconciliation (L54), the structural fix: a verdict is
  rendered only when the parsed count equals mypy's own "Found N errors"
  tally, or a Success line accompanies a parsed 0. Everything else —
  empty stdout from a crashed run, truncated output, a future format or
  colour change that defeats the regex — exits 2 (infrastructure) in
  every mode INCLUDING --update-baseline, which now refuses to write a
  baseline from output it cannot reconcile.

The reconciliation is what makes this durable rather than a patch for one
env var: any future route to unparseable output fails LOUD as a broken
instrument instead of OPEN as a clean surface. Live A/B on this shell:
doctored all-zeros baseline -> exit 1 REGRESSION (was exit 0); real
baseline -> 672 (baseline 672, delta +0) with FORCE_COLOR=3 still set.

Eight new tests pin the truth table: colorized output counted not zeroed
(both the passing and the blocking direction), tally mismatch / missing
tally / empty output / contradictory Success-plus-errors all exit 2, a
genuine Success line still reads as the legitimate 0 the drain is aiming
for, and --update-baseline over garbage writes nothing.

Found while a "surface shrank" report contradicted a 672-delta-0 reading
taken minutes earlier in the same session; the exactly-zero parse on data
that obviously contains something is L53's oldest tell.

